# Engine container crontab, read by supercronic (see deploy/engine.Dockerfile).
#
# CRON_TZ makes every schedule below interpreted in US Eastern time, DST
# included (supercronic loads this via Go's IANA tzdata, which the
# python:3.13-slim base image already ships). This is the whole point of
# moving off host cron: Debian host cron has no CRON_TZ, which is why
# scripts/paper.sh's ET slot guard and the old crontab's EDT/EST line-pair
# convention existed at all (see docs/architecture.md and docs/operations.md
# for that history). Under supercronic, ONE line per job at its real ET time
# is correct year-round — no pairs, no guard needed. The slot-guard argument
# is still passed to market-hours jobs below anyway, as a belt-and-suspenders
# check: if this file's TZ handling is ever misconfigured, a job fires at
# the wrong wall-clock time and the guard makes it a loud no-op instead of a
# silent wrong-time trade, exactly as it did on the old host-cron schedule.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York

# --- Confirmed against the live server's real `crontab -l`, captured
#     2026-08-17 (supersedes an earlier, partially-wrong log-based
#     reconstruction — see git history if you need the old guesses) --------

