# check the day this file went live. Caught by diffing against real
# `crontab -l` before cutover, not by any automated check.
55 9  * * 1-5 /app/scripts/paper.sh health 09:55
59 9  * * 1-5 /app/scripts/paper.sh health2x 09:59
5  16 * * 1-5 /app/scripts/paper.sh health 16:05
9  16 * * 1-5 /app/scripts/paper.sh health2x 16:09

# momls2x: unslotted (not market-hours sensitive — see scripts/paper.sh's
# case statement). Real crontab line is `0 6 * * 3` (UTC, no CRON_TZ) —
# under EDT that's 02:00 ET Wednesday; under EST it drifts to 01:00 ET
# since a raw UTC cron line can't track DST the way CRON_TZ does here.
# Pinned to the EDT reading (02:00 ET) — an hour of seasonal drift is
# immaterial for an off-hours data rebuild, same reasoning as `weekly`
# below. (An earlier version of this file guessed Thursday 15:44 ET from a
# single observed firing during an unusually heavy upgrade-testing week;
# that guess was wrong on both the day and the hour — replaced here with
# the real schedule read directly off the server.)
0  2  * * 3 /app/scripts/paper.sh momls2x

# weekly: unslotted. Real crontab line is `5 22 * * 0` UTC — 18:05 ET under
# EDT, 17:05 ET under EST. Close enough to this file's prior 18:00 ET
# placeholder that no change was needed; kept as-is.
0  18 * * 0 /app/scripts/paper.sh weekly

# shadows2x (own lock; see docs/architecture.md) is a real, working job in
# scripts/paper.sh but is deliberately NOT scheduled here: it does not
# appear anywhere in the real server crontab, so it has never actually run
# in production. An earlier version of this file guessed a schedule for it
# and would have started running it for the first time as an unannounced
# side effect of this migration. Confirmed with the operator (2026-08-17):
# leave it off. Add a line here deliberately, as its own reviewed change,
# if it should ever go live.

# iwmfwd: real crontab line is `30 23 * * *` UTC (no day restriction) —
# 19:30 ET under EDT, 18:30 ET under EST. Not market-hours sensitive, so
# either reading is fine; pinned to the EDT reading like momls2x above.
# (An earlier version of this file claimed iwmfwd had no server-side
# schedule at all and proposed inventing one at 20:30 ET — wrong: it's
# already live, just off by about an hour from the placeholder.)
30 19 * * * /app/scripts/paper.sh iwmfwd
